Subject: [PATCH 13/24] ALSA: hda/ca0132: AE-9: enable What U Hear capture

Set the WUH connection point to 48 kHz in ae9_dsp_defaults; without it the
What U Hear capture device (2) stayed silent. Tested: a 440 Hz playback is
captured at -26 dBFS.

install/20-ae9-inputs.conf exposes the rear line-in (hw:Creative,4) and
What U Hear (hw:Creative,2) as separate PipeWire sources so Audacity/OBS
can select them; install.sh/uninstall.sh manage the file. README documents
the three capture paths and the Audacity 128-channel default-device quirk.

Signed-off-by: DarkNikGr <mitakidisnikos@gmail.com>
---
 sound/hda/codecs/ca0132.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sound/hda/codecs/ca0132.c b/sound/hda/codecs/ca0132.c
index 2fa1d15..75b1328 100644
--- a/sound/hda/codecs/ca0132.c
+++ b/sound/hda/codecs/ca0132.c
@@ -9551,6 +9551,7 @@ static void ae9_dsp_defaults(struct hda_codec *codec)
 	dspio_set_uint_param(codec, 0x96, 0x3c, FLOAT_ZERO);
 	dspio_set_uint_param(codec, 0x31, 0x00, FLOAT_TWO);
 	dspio_set_uint_param(codec, 0x32, 0x00, FLOAT_TWO);
+	chipio_set_conn_rate(codec, MEM_CONNID_WUH, SR_48_000);
 }
 
